{"c":[{"id":"c539feeaf5360a4d","sum":"W3: XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply. Memory markdown: MemoryStore(dir) uses <dir>/Memory (real folder only without --data-dir) and grants no authority (that stays in memory.sqlite). oxc rejects raw U+2028 in a regex; write \\u2028.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"569740c12f8fdab5","sum":"W3: client setCodeSigningRequirement blocks what it receives, not its first call; XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply. Memory is markdown: MemoryStore(dir) uses <dir>/Memory; main.ts uses the real folder only without --data-dir.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-a08d2817ff5ece3d","text":"W3: NSXPCConnection.setCodeSigningRequirement on the client blocks what it receives, not its own first call; whoever owns the Mach name sees open's arguments, so XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204904Z-98cc6d5ebfceb30a","text":"Personal memory is markdown (helper/src/memory): MemoryStore(dir) keeps it in <dir>/Memory unless told otherwise, and main.ts uses ~/Library/Application Support/Caret/Memory only when --data-dir is not given, so tests and evals never open the real folder.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6e639a4926698b7e","sum":"Memory markdown grants no authority (permissions, onItsOwn, hand-off stay in memory.sqlite); editing a skill file puts it back on Tab (SkillJson.fileDigest). oxc rejects a raw U+2028/U+2029 in a regex literal; write the \\u2028 escape (Write tools may unescape it).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204920Z-024f4219fb18c6cf","text":"Memory markdown grants no authority: permissions and a skill's onItsOwn, clean runs and hand-off stay in memory.sqlite; editing a skill's file puts it back on Tab, and SkillJson.fileDigest catches edits made while Caret was stopped.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204920Z-0ba29fff62387456","text":"vite's oxc parser rejects a regex literal holding a raw U+2028/U+2029 (a line terminator); write the \\u2028 escape. An agent's Write tool can turn the escape into the raw character.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e60e3e751e2435c2","sum":"Remotes and Groq writers: push v2/* only to remote sam; Ask intents use gpt-oss-120b, plan programs qwen3.8 (about 1,000 output tokens a minute and 200k a day); space writer calls with a fresh AbortSignal after each wait. U+2731 marks required labels on the job form.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e2ebd6c0099fdfde","sum":"Push v2/* only to remote sam (SamGu-NRX/Caret); origin is the team hackathon repo. Ask intents use INTENT_ROUTE (gpt-oss-120b), plan programs WRITER_ROUTE (qwen3.8, ~1,000 output tokens/min, 200k/day on Groq); gpt-oss strict json_schema can 400.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T210855Z-22a0908ac8155d26","text":"Push v2/* branches to the remote named sam (SamGu-NRX/Caret), where their PRs live. origin is the team hackathon repo (theodorexli/hackathon-2026-09-19); a bare 'git push origin' publishes there.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T211051Z-2bd567d78f578d5c","text":"B25: Ask intents go to INTENT_ROUTE (gpt-oss-120b), plan programs to WRITER_ROUTE (qwen3.8); qwen3.8's Groq 200k tokens/day ran out during dev runs, and gpt-oss strict json_schema can 400 'does not match the expected schema'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b1d476e32a92cb95","sum":"B25: writers that space calls must give each request a fresh AbortSignal after the wait (a 15 s gap aborted every call); the job form marks required labels with U+2731, which realfill normLabel strips.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T211051Z-3925313f151b5275","text":"B25: eval writers that space calls must give the request a fresh AbortSignal after the wait; a 15 s gap aborted every intent in planner-eval's first GUI run.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T211051Z-9174d67891bff255","text":"B25: the job form marks required labels with U+2731; realfill normLabel strips it, and B24's scoreboards counted those four fields as not found.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
